          "section": "2.2.3. Creep resistance model",
          "quote": "It is known [32] that the second generation alloy CMSX-4 is one of the most successful alloys that has been extensively used in aero and industry turbine applications, which has shown an excellent combination of high temperature strength and phase stability. This can be attributed to its close to optimum microstructural architecture [2], including ~70 vol.% of γ′ phase and an appropriate γ/γ′ misfit to confer cuboidal γ′ precipitates with a uniform size of ~0.5 μm after heat treatment.",
